d "ad58d20a-321f-5920-925e-1ef527d5406d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103894" :question/problem "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-3x-4y=0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-3x-4y & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-3x)+({y}^{2}-4y) & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & =\\frac{25}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect square and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & ={(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(\\frac{3}{2},2)$ and its radius is $\\frac{5}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103894/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98e3f3b4-8dfa-515c-90b1-09fb19d68144"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103894"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76374/selection/c70944d2c6679533a3f923066c4663ad36320579f722bbe28d8a605b6cb1845b" :answer/id #uuid "14880970-af68-5240-862b-98f07eb9db43" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "center: $(\\frac{1}{4},1),$ radius: $\\frac{7}{4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76374/selection/abcad4a00e1fc0b71af00aae6cfbcf761ccec21276793413e48c71b2acf15b28" :answer/id #uuid "3f1a59f5-ac1d-522e-b6fb-7bb4e1fbc3ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "center: $(1,\\frac{1}{4}),$ radius: $\\frac{3}{4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76374/selection/499317ed691a3cc7188d16fd061dc5bfda82fdb262d8b129b6275d670bc1ad4c" :answer/id #uuid "9169325b-3dfc-533a-b438-cd09ce7895a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "center: $(-1,-\\frac{1}{4}),$ radius: $\\frac{3}{4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/valida